{"record": "end", "run_id": "20261116T082545Z_dev-03_flat_f751", "reason": "answered", "detail": "", "answer": {"answer": "In Kim, Lee, Park and Shin (arXiv:1601.05089), the best fit for ψψ̄ → h2h2 (via ψψ̄ → h2 → h2h2) used m_ψ = 69.2 GeV and m_h2 = 35.7 GeV. They gave ⟨σv⟩ = 2.26×10⁻²⁶ cm³ s⁻¹. The canonical J-factor was rescaled by 𝒥 = 2.2, so J̄ = 2.2 × J̄_canonical. This fit has χ² = 23.19 (p-value 0.39). Also, 2×10²³ GeV²/cm⁵ is the canonical J̄ the paper quotes for its region of interest.", "found": true, "evidence": [{"arxiv_id": "1601.05089v3", "section_id": "3.4"}, {"arxiv_id": "1601.05089v3", "section_id": "3"}, {"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "7.2"}]}, "turns": 3, "seconds": 9.923, "tool_calls": 3, "tool_result_chars": 198344, "input_tokens": 8, "output_tokens": 639, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 87833, "cache_read_input_tokens": 70945, "parser_versions": ["4"], "response_models": ["claude-sonnet-5-5"], "ended_at": "2026-11-16T08:25:55+00:00"}
